 "kept_on_synth": {
  "status.burn": "No fire crackle exists in any of the six packs. The closest family (scratch) centres at 6401-12076 Hz against a 2389 Hz target - a high scrape, not a burn - and every other candidate is a 5-second engine loop. The synth voice is a filtered noise burst at 1800 Hz, which is already the right shape."
 },
 "processing": "mono + trim(-40 dBFS, faded) + per-cue duration cap (faded) + smallest-bytes MP3 encode among bandwidth-legal sample rates + peak-match to the replaced synth cue. See tools/audio-pipeline/process_all.py. The four ui.* cues run the same steps through tools/audio-pipeline/process_ui.py, whose only difference is where the peak-match reference comes from: a UI synth voice is a single tone(), so its peak IS its gain argument and needs no re-render to measure.",
 "music_note": "Provenance for the design/11 music loops, kept SEPARATE from `cues` above and outside `packs.json`: `packs.json` declares every SFX source pack CC0 and `audioAssets.test.ts` asserts that of every entry, and five of these six tracks are CC-BY, which REQUIRES a credit the SFX never needed. Since 2026-10-06 every track is openly licensed music written by people (the 2026-08-31 Suno masters were judged not good enough by the owner and are gone). Allowed licences are CC0 and CC-BY only: both permit commercial use and an edited loop; NC is out because the game earns from ads, ND because cutting a loop region IS an adaptation, and SA is avoided. Each record names its upstream URL and SHA-256, so the full master can be fetched back; `source` under art/audio/sources/ is either that upstream file verbatim or an EXCERPT (the loop region plus 5 s either side, re-encoded to Vorbis), because the upstream downloads run to 20-50 MB. `region_start_s` is in the ARCHIVED file's seconds; `excerpt_start_s` places it in the upstream file. `attribution` is the exact line the game shows (Settings, AUDIO), and `client/src/audio/musicAssets.test.ts` holds it equal to `client/src/audio/musicCredits.ts`. `tools/audio-pipeline/process_music.py` cuts the loops and `audit.py --class music` gates the result.",
