   "rationale": "Chapter 3's run bed (the Storm Descent, lightning). A driving electronic piece, the composer's looping version; 50.0 s from 27.5 s of its 96.0 s, band-diff 1.21 dB with the shelf on the upstream file, 1.20 dB as shipped. Picked from 16 measured CC0/CC-BY candidates: its overlap material is uncorrelated (+0.06, so the equal-power fade moves the level +0.3 dB), at 120 bpm every 0.5 s length keeps both decks' beat grids aligned through the fade, L/R correlation +0.49 is mono-safe, and its 2-8 kHz band sits where boss and ember do. 'Electric Exodus' (FoxSynergy) closed at 1.05 dB but is 10 dB brighter in 2-8 kHz than any shipped bed, near-mono, and its two decks' drums flam by 80 ms at the crossfade unless the loop is cut to an off-grid 52.92 s; 'Blitz Kaskade' and 'Thunderous Fall' repeat (0.0-0.4 dB) and their overlaps correlate +0.4-0.9, swelling 1.0-1.9 dB. Kept to 50 s for the music subpackage's 3 MB. The 80 Hz / -10 dB shelf: 20-250 Hz sat 6.2 dB above the mids. The credit line is the author's own format plus the licence.",
