   "rationale": "Chapter 4's run bed (the Blight Descent, poison: the finale, the source of the crystallising contamination). A dark, beatless suspense piece, the composer's looping version; 49.5 s from 15.0 s of its 99.7 s, band-diff 0.67 dB on the upstream file, 0.65 dB as shipped. Picked from 38 measured CC0/CC-BY candidates: its overlap material is uncorrelated (+0.05, so the equal-power fade moves the level +0.14 dB), it has no beat to flam (onset-envelope correlation 0.15 at best), L/R correlation +0.28 is mono-safe, and at 2-8 kHz 25.0 dB under the mids it is the darkest run bed, below every cue. 'Lightless Dawn' (Kevin MacLeod) closed at 0.53 dB with a +0.7 dB swell and needed the shelf; 'Gathering Darkness' (Kevin MacLeod) closed at 0.38 dB but its overlap anti-correlates (-0.31); 'They're Here' (Eric Matyas) could not close under 1.4 dB near 50 s. No shelf: 20-250 Hz sits 4.2 dB above the mids, under the 5.3-6.4 dB that got one. The page's licence field reads CC-BY 3.0 and the author's notice CC BY 4.0; the capture records both, and the credit line is the author's own format plus the licence.",
